{"invocation_id": "82035881-9b01-4e19-9214-a41db64eea28", "client_id": 140204234762128, "wrapper_id": 140204235316112, "request": {"messages": [{"content": "\nmanager. Use the available tools to solve plant-related tasks.\n\nInstructions:\n1. Begin by creating a clear, step-by-step plan for the task. Provide an explanation of each step before proceeding. You may refine the plan as needed based on intermediate results.\n2. When using multiple tools, be sure to provide the outputs from one tool to the next as inputs if necessary.\n3. When you need to use coding-related tools, provide clear descriptions of the task requirements and expected outputs. Do not pass concrete codes to the coding related functions.\n4. When you need to use computer vision to solve a task, first check the available checkpoints using the 'get_model_zoo' function:\n    - Select a suitable checkpoint for the task if it it exists. Make sure you pass a list of image paths (e.g. [./data/image1.png, ./data/image2.png, ...]), or a single csv/json file (e.g. ./data/metadata.json) to the corresponding inference function.\n    - If no suitable checkpoint is available, suggest user to finetune a new model. DO NOT rely on online source. Use the 'get_dataset_format' function to instruct the user to provide a training dataset.\n5. When a user ask you to execute a saved pipeline, first call 'get_pipeline_zoo' to know what pipelines are available, and then call 'get_pipeline_info' to understand how to use the selected pipeline.\n6. At the end of the task, provide a summary of the results and ask the user if they need any further assistance.\n    \nReturn \"TERMINATE\" when the task is completed.\n", "role": "system"}, {"content": "\nGiven ./results/Case1/aracrop_phenotypes.csv, compute and plot the mean and standard deviation of these phenotypes [leaf count, projected leaf area (PLA), plant diameter, plant perimeter] for each ecotype on every day after sowing.\nSave one plot for each phenotype in the ./results/Case1_Task2_wlog directory, naming them as [phenotype]_plot.png, e.g. pla_plot.png.\nFor each plot:\n- Use shades to represent the standard deviation.\n- Set plot title as \"Mean and STD of [phenotype] for each ecotype over time\".\n- Set x-axis label as \"Days after sowing\".\n- Set y-axis label as \"[phenotype]\".\n- Set legend to show the ecotype names.\n- Do not use grid lines.\n", "role": "user", "name": "Admin"}, {"tool_calls": [{"id": "call_ac6VWASMfOCokVp0aUOgkuDT", "function": {"arguments": "{\"dir_path\":\"./results/Case1_Task2_wlog\"}", "name": "make_dir"}, "type": "function"}], "content": null, "role": "assistant"}, {"tool_call_id": "call_ac6VWASMfOCokVp0aUOgkuDT", "role": "tool", "content": "Directory './results/Case1_Task2_wlog' already exists."}, {"tool_calls": [{"id": "call_MG2eOraTH8OS8yHQrhFvAbUS", "function": {"arguments": "{\"message\": \"Compute the mean and standard deviation of leaf count for each ecotype on every day after sowing.\", \"file_path\": \"./results/Case1/aracrop_phenotypes.csv\", \"save_path\": \"./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/leaf_count_stats.csv\"}", "name": "compute_from_csv"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_EwDiv8XE5LHM4xokHYgXDqlF", "function": {"arguments": "{\"message\": \"Compute the mean and standard deviation of projected leaf area (PLA) for each ecotype on every day after sowing.\", \"file_path\": \"./results/Case1/aracrop_phenotypes.csv\", \"save_path\": \"./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/pla_stats.csv\"}", "name": "compute_from_csv"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_26Yg2hJXHX1TNj3Zjporu47R", "function": {"arguments": "{\"message\": \"Compute the mean and standard deviation of plant diameter for each ecotype on every day after sowing.\", \"file_path\": \"./results/Case1/aracrop_phenotypes.csv\", \"save_path\": \"./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/plant_diameter_stats.csv\"}", "name": "compute_from_csv"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_StzkvPmBFv125T0RnM4V5QKW", "function": {"arguments": "{\"message\": \"Compute the mean and standard deviation of plant perimeter for each ecotype on every day after sowing.\", \"file_path\": \"./results/Case1/aracrop_phenotypes.csv\", \"save_path\": \"./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/plant_perimeter_stats.csv\"}", "name": "compute_from_csv"}, "type": "function"}], "content": null, "role": "assistant"}, {"tool_call_id": "call_MG2eOraTH8OS8yHQrhFvAbUS", "role": "tool", "content": "The new csv is saved at ./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/leaf_count_stats.csv. Here is an explanation of the operation process: Certainly! Let's break down the process in simple terms:\n\n1. **Understanding the Task**: The goal was to find out the average number of leaves and how much this number varies for different plant types on each day after they were planted.\n\n2. **Organizing the Information**: We started by looking at the data, which included details about plant types, the number of days since planting, and the number of leaves.\n\n3. **Grouping the Data**: We sorted the information based on plant type and the number of days since planting. This helped us focus on each specific group separately.\n\n4. **Calculating Averages and Variations**: For each group, we calculated two things:\n   - The average number of leaves, which gives a general idea of leaf growth.\n   - The variation in leaf numbers, which shows how much the leaf count differs within the group.\n\n5. **Saving the Results**: Finally, we saved these findings in a file so that they can be easily accessed and reviewed later.\n\nBy following these steps, we were able to summarize the leaf growth patterns for different plant types over time.."}, {"tool_call_id": "call_EwDiv8XE5LHM4xokHYgXDqlF", "role": "tool", "content": "The new csv is saved at ./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/pla_stats.csv. Here is an explanation of the operation process: Certainly! Let's break down the process in simple terms:\n\n1. **Understanding the Task**: The goal was to find out the average size and the variation in size of leaves for different plant types on each day after they were planted.\n\n2. **Organizing the Information**: We started by looking at the data, which included details about the type of plant, the number of days since planting, and the size of the leaves.\n\n3. **Calculating the Averages and Variations**: For each type of plant and each day after planting, we calculated two things:\n   - The average size of the leaves.\n   - How much the leaf sizes varied from this average.\n\n4. **Storing the Results**: Once we had these calculations, we organized them neatly into a table. This table showed the plant type, the day after planting, the average leaf size, and the variation in size.\n\n5. **Saving the Information**: Finally, we saved this organized information into a file so it could be easily accessed and used later.\n\nThis approach allowed us to systematically analyze and store important information about the growth patterns of different plant types over time.."}, {"tool_call_id": "call_26Yg2hJXHX1TNj3Zjporu47R", "role": "tool", "content": "The new csv is saved at ./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/plant_diameter_stats.csv. Here is an explanation of the operation process: Certainly! Let's break down the process in simple terms:\n\n1. **Understanding the Task**: The goal was to find out the average size and the variation in size of plants for each type of plant on each day after they were planted.\n\n2. **Organizing the Information**: We started by looking at the information we had, which included details about different types of plants, the days since they were planted, and their sizes.\n\n3. **Grouping the Data**: We organized this information by grouping it based on the type of plant and the number of days since planting. This way, we could look at each group separately.\n\n4. **Calculating the Averages and Variations**: For each group, we calculated two things:\n   - The average size of the plants, which gives us an idea of how big the plants are getting on average.\n   - The variation in size, which tells us how much the sizes differ from one another within the same group.\n\n5. **Saving the Results**: Finally, we saved these findings in a file so that they can be easily accessed and reviewed later.\n\nBy following these steps, we were able to provide a clear picture of how plant sizes change over time for different types of plants.."}, {"tool_call_id": "call_StzkvPmBFv125T0RnM4V5QKW", "role": "tool", "content": "The new csv is saved at ./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/plant_perimeter_stats.csv. Here is an explanation of the operation process: Certainly! Let's break down the process in simple terms:\n\n1. **Understanding the Task**: The goal was to find out the average size and the variation in size of plant perimeters for different types of plants on each day after they were planted.\n\n2. **Organizing the Information**: We started by organizing the information we had about the plants. This involved looking at the type of plant and how many days it had been since they were planted.\n\n3. **Calculating Averages and Variations**: For each type of plant and each day, we calculated two things:\n   - The average size of the plant perimeter, which gives us an idea of the typical size.\n   - The variation in size, which tells us how much the sizes differ from one another.\n\n4. **Saving the Results**: Once we had these calculations, we saved them in a file so that they could be easily accessed and reviewed later.\n\n5. **Presenting the Findings**: Finally, we prepared the results in a way that makes it easy to understand and use, showing the average and variation for each plant type and day.\n\nThis approach helps in understanding how plant sizes change over time and how they differ between different types of plants.."}, {"tool_calls": [{"id": "call_gno1SjP434ma9B3XTflTbBCZ", "function": {"arguments": "{\"message\": \"Plot the mean and standard deviation of leaf count for each ecotype over time. Use shades to represent the standard deviation. Set plot title as 'Mean and STD of leaf count for each ecotype over time'. Set x-axis label as 'Days after sowing'. Set y-axis label as 'Leaf count'. Set legend to show the ecotype names. Do not use grid lines.\", \"file_path\": \"./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/leaf_count_stats.csv\", \"save_path\": \"./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/leaf_count_plot.png\"}", "name": "plot_from_csv"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_MSYehN4O7KpLu0ihFOslQQG9", "function": {"arguments": "{\"message\": \"Plot the mean and standard deviation of projected leaf area (PLA) for each ecotype over time. Use shades to represent the standard deviation. Set plot title as 'Mean and STD of projected leaf area (PLA) for each ecotype over time'. Set x-axis label as 'Days after sowing'. Set y-axis label as 'Projected leaf area (PLA)'. Set legend to show the ecotype names. Do not use grid lines.\", \"file_path\": \"./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/pla_stats.csv\", \"save_path\": \"./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/pla_plot.png\"}", "name": "plot_from_csv"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_c8fOZWnebJcmkTm7nZi9Rfvu", "function": {"arguments": "{\"message\": \"Plot the mean and standard deviation of plant diameter for each ecotype over time. Use shades to represent the standard deviation. Set plot title as 'Mean and STD of plant diameter for each ecotype over time'. Set x-axis label as 'Days after sowing'. Set y-axis label as 'Plant diameter'. Set legend to show the ecotype names. Do not use grid lines.\", \"file_path\": \"./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/plant_diameter_stats.csv\", \"save_path\": \"./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/plant_diameter_plot.png\"}", "name": "plot_from_csv"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_vY651OUYFFF4TGjvS69CKfki", "function": {"arguments": "{\"message\": \"Plot the mean and standard deviation of plant perimeter for each ecotype over time. Use shades to represent the standard deviation. Set plot title as 'Mean and STD of plant perimeter for each ecotype over time'. Set x-axis label as 'Days after sowing'. Set y-axis label as 'Plant perimeter'. Set legend to show the ecotype names. Do not use grid lines.\", \"file_path\": \"./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/plant_perimeter_stats.csv\", \"save_path\": \"./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/plant_perimeter_plot.png\"}", "name": "plot_from_csv"}, "type": "function"}], "content": null, "role": "assistant"}, {"tool_call_id": "call_gno1SjP434ma9B3XTflTbBCZ", "role": "tool", "content": "The task was successfully completed. A plot showing the mean and standard deviation of leaf count for each ecotype over time was generated. The mean leaf count is represented by lines, and the standard deviation is represented by shaded areas around these lines. The plot includes a title, axis labels, and a legend indicating the ecotype names. The plot was saved to the specified path: `./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/leaf_count_plot.png`."}, {"tool_call_id": "call_MSYehN4O7KpLu0ihFOslQQG9", "role": "tool", "content": "The task involved plotting the mean and standard deviation of projected leaf area (PLA) for each ecotype over time using data from a CSV file. The plot was successfully generated with the mean PLA values represented as lines and the standard deviation as shaded areas around these lines. The plot includes a title, axis labels, and a legend for the ecotype names. The plot was saved to the specified path: `./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/pla_plot.png`."}, {"tool_call_id": "call_c8fOZWnebJcmkTm7nZi9Rfvu", "role": "tool", "content": "The task involved plotting the mean and standard deviation of plant diameter for each ecotype over time using data from a CSV file. The plot was successfully created with the mean values represented by lines and the standard deviation represented by shaded areas around the lines. The plot includes a title, labeled axes, and a legend indicating the ecotype names. The plot was saved to the specified path without grid lines.\n\nThe saved plot can be found at: `./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/plant_diameter_plot.png`."}, {"tool_call_id": "call_vY651OUYFFF4TGjvS69CKfki", "role": "tool", "content": "The task involved plotting the mean and standard deviation of plant perimeter for each ecotype over time using data from a CSV file. The plot was successfully created with the mean values represented by lines and the standard deviation represented by shaded areas around these lines. The plot includes a title, axis labels, and a legend for the ecotype names. Grid lines were not included as per the instructions. The plot was saved to the specified path.\n\nThe saved plot can be found at: `./results/Case1_Task2_wlog/plant_perimeter_plot.png`."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Perform Mixed-design Repeated Measures ANOVA on given data (Greenhouse-Geisser correction will be automatically applied if needed)", "name": "perform_anova", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"data_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Path to the input CSV file"}, "descriptor": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the descriptor column to analyse"}, "within_subject_factor": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the within-subjects factor"}, "between_subject_factor": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the between-subjects factor"}, "subject_id": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the subject identifier"}, "save_path": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Path to save the ANOVA results CSV"}}, "required": ["data_path", "descriptor", "within_subject_factor", "between_subject_factor", "subject_id"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Perform Post-hoc Tukey-Kramer test on given data", "name": "perform_tukey_test", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"data_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Path to the input CSV file"}, "descriptor": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the descriptor column to analyse"}, "between_subject_factor": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the between-subjects factor"}, "subject_id": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the subject identifier"}, "save_path": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Path to save the Tukey-Kramer results CSV"}}, "required": ["data_path", "descriptor", "between_subject_factor", "subject_id"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Extract and save a reproducible pipeline from chat history. Ask user to provide a name for the pipeline.", "name": "extract_pipeline", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"pipeline_name": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the pipeline to be saved."}, "chat_log_path": {"type": "string", "default": "./autogen_logs/runtime.log", "description": "The path to the chat log file."}}, "required": ["pipeline_name"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Get the information of all registered pipelines. It is useful when a user wants to know what pipelines are available before executing any.", "name": "get_pipeline_zoo", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {}, "required": []}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Get the information of a specific pipeline. This is useful for you to know how to use a pipeline selected by the user, including the description, arguments, and output type.", "name": "get_pipeline_info", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"pipeline_name": {"type": "string", "description": "Name of pipeline to be queried."}}, "required": ["pipeline_name"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Execute a saved pipeline from the pipeline zoo. Before executing a pipeline, you must call 'get_pipeline_zoo' to know what pipelines are available, and call 'get_pipeline_info' to understand how to use the selected pipeline.", "name": "execute_pipeline", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"pipeline_name": {"type": "string", "description": "Name of pipeline to be called."}, "kwargs": {"type": "object", "description": "Arguments of the selected pipeline."}}, "required": ["pipeline_name", "kwargs"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Perform basic arithmetic operations between two integers.", "name": "calculator", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"a": {"type": "integer", "description": "a"}, "b": {"type": "integer", "description": "b"}, "operator": {"type": "string", "description": "operator"}}, "required": ["a", "b", "operator"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Search and scrape content from the web. Results are returned in a dictionary. Useful when you need to find information on a specific topic.", "name": "google_search", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"query": {"type": "string", "description": "query"}, "num_results": {"type": "integer", "default": 10, "description": "num_results"}}, "required": ["query"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Check available computer vision checkpoints. Must be called before using computer vision models.", "name": "get_model_zoo", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {}, "required": []}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Perform instance segmentation on plant images", "name": "infer_instance_segmentation", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"image_urls": {"anyOf": [{"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "List of image paths"}, "file_path": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Path to CSV/JSON file with a 'file_name' column/key containing image URLs"}, "checkpoint": {"type": "string", "default": null, "description": "Segmentation model checkpoint identifier."}, "batch_size": {"type": "integer", "default": 1, "description": "Number of images to process per batch."}, "device": {"type": "string", "default": "cuda", "description": "Device to use for inference ('cuda' or 'cpu')."}, "output_dir": {"type": "string", "default": "./results", "description": "Directory path to save results."}}, "required": []}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Perform image classification on plant images", "name": "infer_image_classification", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"image_urls": {"anyOf": [{"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "List of image paths"}, "file_path": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Path to CSV/JSON file with a 'file_name' column/key containing image URLs"}, "checkpoint": {"type": "string", "default": null, "description": "Classification model checkpoint identifier."}, "batch_size": {"type": "integer", "default": 1, "description": "Number of images to process per batch."}, "device": {"type": "string", "default": "cuda", "description": "Device to use for inference ('cuda' or 'cpu')."}, "output_dir": {"type": "string", "default": "./results", "description": "Directory path to save results."}}, "required": []}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Perform image regression on plant images", "name": "infer_image_regression", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"image_urls": {"anyOf": [{"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "List of image paths"}, "file_path": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Path to CSV/JSON file with a 'file_name' column/key containing image URLs"}, "checkpoint": {"type": "string", "default": null, "description": "Regression model checkpoint identifier."}, "batch_size": {"type": "integer", "default": 1, "description": "Number of images to process per batch."}, "device": {"type": "string", "default": "cuda", "description": "Device to use for inference ('cuda' or 'cpu')."}, "output_dir": {"type": "string", "default": "./results", "description": "Directory path to save results."}}, "required": []}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Compute phenotypes from an instance segmentation result file", "name": "compute_phenotypes_from_ins_seg", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"ins_seg_result_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Path to a COCO format JSON file containing instance segmentation results."}, "save_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Path to save the computed phenotypes."}, "pixel_to_cm": {"type": "number", "default": 1.0, "description": "The scale to map pixel values to cm. i.e. number of pixels * pixel_to_cm = cm."}}, "required": ["ins_seg_result_path", "save_path"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Write and execute code to solve tasks. Please provide a complete task description rather than concrete code as the input to this function.", "name": "coding", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"message": {"type": "string", "description": "Describe the task to be solved."}, "file_path": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "(Optional) The path to an input csv file."}}, "required": ["message"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Analyse a plot using GPT-4o.", "name": "analyse_plot", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"message": {"type": "string", "description": "The request of analysing a plot. e.g. 'what plant yields the most leaves at the end of the experiment?'"}, "file_path": {"type": "string", "description": "The path of the plot to be analysed, including the suffix."}}, "required": ["message", "file_path"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Compute statistics or new values from a CSV file. Optionally, it saves the results to a new file.", "name": "compute_from_csv", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"message": {"type": "string", "description": "The request of computing from a CSV file. Example: 'Compute the average of A for B on C.'"}, "file_path": {"type":